  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Supporting International Dialogue on Accountability for Ukraine Phase II: Secretariat Dialogue Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To support the Dialogue Group Secretariat providing needs-based technical support to the Dialogue Group workstreams and their respective Co-Chairs. 2) To maintain secure and reliable rules, techniques, and environment for the workstream related data storage and exchange. 3) To support the Dialogue Group Secretariat with facilitation of a more active and practical participation of the Prosecutor General&#x2019;s Office (PGO) mid-level management in the workstreams. 4) To enhance the role of the Dialogue Group in facilitating proper and timely addressing of issues concerning accountability for international crimes. 5) To enhance visibility and public awareness of the Dialogue Group&#x2019;s work.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ukrainian Prosecutor General&#x2019;s Office (PGO); Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Ukraine (MFA); Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Government of the Netherlands (Dutch MFA); the International Criminal Court (ICC); the European Union Agency for Criminal Justice Cooperation (EuroJust); the European Commission (EC); States and local and international civil coalitions acting in their capacity as workstream Co-Chairs and Plenary Dialogue Group members.Indirect beneficiaries: Wider population of Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to continue advancing international dialogue on accountability in Ukraine by facilitating coordination, coherence and complementarity between civil society and Ukrainian institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
